{"card_hash": "b4539bf48feaa45d092df1dc98bff44c562d81402c03faac73ba65f61b4cd328", "channel": "Dwarkesh Patel", "chars": 75184, "chars_all_clips": 75184, "chars_chosen_clips": 1440, "clip_count": 85, "clips": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=101", "end": 204.16, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "899084656dd7b173c80c0f0c81e350300a727883b755415c357093e0e64c243f", "start": 101.36, "text": "Up until now, they have been companies that mostly lost money. Anthropic started turning a profit in Q2. It’s believed at some point in Q3, OpenAI could start turning a profit even, with the bigger rise of Codex and 5.6 and all this. But if", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=877", "end": 956.08, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "07b655a1141791ff3461dbbc639d855f1def3081435cb596d1c2d3733e677a86", "start": 877.04, "text": "Go get a GB300 rack, go download the Kimi weights, go download vLLM or SGLang, set it up. Codex and Fable can actually help you do this. It’s pretty simple. It’s not trivial, but it’s not rocket science. Go put it on OpenRouter. It’s very s", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=1715", "end": 1781.52, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "600725843ef820b68d1ccef9cdffc4c617764b4142088949961f21c1872cbccf", "start": 1715.76, "text": "Obviously, who captures the value is still up for debate, but ultimately everyone’s going to raise their prices. Because they can, and it’s super inflationary. Especially if the method of regulation is… Right now, so far, it’s just \"don’t r", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=2670", "end": 2746.08, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "09638001dc44956b1f7e2ac830ce1bfe9c77264c8fc09d5ee9de90ace3196b9e", "start": 2670.32, "text": "But still, at the current size of the US economy, it’ll be like a third to a quarter of the US economy just going towards data centers. As I say that out loud, I’m like, \"Maybe you’re right and we just won’t allow it, and that’s the reason ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=3624", "end": 3680.32, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "f1199de44559761761349de493503f986a5190857a611ffc984b67fde6fbbc0f", "start": 3624.64, "text": "Part of my brain is like, \"It might be hundreds of percent,\" but let’s say it’s at least tens of percent. I’m just like, okay. Every country that is not involved in the production of AI defaults. Every stock that is not an AI stock is worth", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=4032", "end": 4131.12, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "a7e63ef51d0fc21cb04c2847059f8a1d66a1eb759eb1a22eec78272851d89729", "start": 4032.08, "text": "The Jane Street team follows frontier LLM research closely. A relatively common intern project is adapting a recent paper to financial markets, which come with their own set of gnarly problems. Ultimately, we're trying to model thousands of", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "AI and ML", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=101", "end": 204.16, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "899084656dd7b173c80c0f0c81e350300a727883b755415c357093e0e64c243f", "start": 101.36, "text": "Up until now, they have been companies that mostly lost money. Anthropic started turning a profit in Q2. It’s believed at some point in Q3, OpenAI could start turning a profit even, with the bigger rise of Codex and 5.6 and all this. But if", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=877", "end": 956.08, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "07b655a1141791ff3461dbbc639d855f1def3081435cb596d1c2d3733e677a86", "start": 877.04, "text": "Go get a GB300 rack, go download the Kimi weights, go download vLLM or SGLang, set it up. Codex and Fable can actually help you do this. It’s pretty simple. It’s not trivial, but it’s not rocket science. Go put it on OpenRouter. It’s very s", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=1715", "end": 1781.52, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "600725843ef820b68d1ccef9cdffc4c617764b4142088949961f21c1872cbccf", "start": 1715.76, "text": "Obviously, who captures the value is still up for debate, but ultimately everyone’s going to raise their prices. Because they can, and it’s super inflationary. Especially if the method of regulation is… Right now, so far, it’s just \"don’t r", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=2670", "end": 2746.08, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "09638001dc44956b1f7e2ac830ce1bfe9c77264c8fc09d5ee9de90ace3196b9e", "start": 2670.32, "text": "But still, at the current size of the US economy, it’ll be like a third to a quarter of the US economy just going towards data centers. As I say that out loud, I’m like, \"Maybe you’re right and we just won’t allow it, and that’s the reason ", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2092280377255551320#t=3624", "end": 3680.32, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "f1199de44559761761349de493503f986a5190857a611ffc984b67fde6fbbc0f", "start": 3624.64, "text": "Part of my brain is like, \"It might be hundreds of percent,\" but let’s say it’s at least tens of percent. I’m just like, okay. Every country that is not involved in the production of AI defaults. Every stock that is not an AI stock is worth", "timing": "source_cues", "truncate